course: dictionary
lesson: 12751
title: Dun: a plain, dusty colour
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words name colours, and dun is a quiet one. Dun means a dull, greyish-brown colour, like dry earth or an old sack. Writers use it to show that something looks plain and natural, not bright.
explain: «The old barn was painted dun.» You can picture the faded, dusty wall. The word tells you the colour is dull, not shiny or bright.
explain: Dun can also be a noun. A dun is a horse of this colour, often with a darker mane and tail, so «The dun pony trotted across the field» is about a horse. Read the words around it to see which meaning the writer means.
explain: Dun can also be an old verb. To dun someone is to keep asking them firmly to pay money they owe. Check the sentence: is it about a colour, a horse, or money?
fact: Dun is a dull, greyish-brown colour.
fact: «The old barn was painted dun.» means the paint looked plain and dusty.
fact: A dun is a horse of this colour, usually with a darker mane and tail.
fact: «The shop kept duning him for the money he owed.» Here dun is an old verb meaning to keep asking firmly for payment.
fact: In some very casual writing, «dun» is just a spelling of «done».
exercise: «The farmer's coat was dun, the same colour as the mud.» What colour is dun? | *Dull greyish-brown | Deep blue | Sparkling gold | Bright red
exercise: «The dun pony trotted across the field.» What is the dun in this sentence? | A bird | *A horse | A patch of grass | A cloud
exercise: «The dun hills looked dry under the grey sky.» Find and copy one word that names a dull, greyish-brown colour. | hills | *dun | dry | sky
test: «The shop kept duning him for the money he owed.» What does dun mean here? | A horse with a dark mane | *To keep asking firmly for money he owes | To finish a task | A dull, greyish-brown colour
test: Which meaning of dun fits best in «Her dun coat blended into the rocks»? | A horse | *A dull, greyish-brown colour | Money owed | Very bright and shiny
exam: In «The dun fields stretched to the hills», what does dun describe? | *The colour of the fields | A horse that runs over the hills | Money owed by the farmer | A kind of bird that lives in fields
